// PROBE: what does Cozy do with an input that may violate its own declared
// constraint?  This is `named_cache.ds` with the eviction removed from `put`,
// so `put` can add a second row with an existing key and the declared
// uniqueness invariant becomes false.  Everything else is unchanged.
//
// Result (cozy d7b2c0e, default --collection-depth 4):
//   Checking that put preserves (unique Map {n -> (n).k} (cache))...
//   Error: 'put' may not preserve invariant (unique Map {n -> (n).k} (cache))
// and it REFUSES to synthesize.  See README "What Cozy does with a spec whose
// constraint can break".
NamedCacheViolating:
    type Node = { k : String, size : Int }
    state cache : Bag<Node>
    invariant unique [n.k | n <- cache];
    query get(key : String)
        the [n | n <- cache, n.k == key]
    op put(node : Node)
        cache.add(node);
